        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Payment hygiene rules</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">OKAD's creator operations team has processed thousands of creator payments. These rules prevent the most common payment problems:</p>
        <ul class="pl-5 mb-4 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
          <li><strong>Invoice immediately upon delivery</strong> &mdash; do not wait for brand approval to send the invoice. Attach the deliverable and the invoice in the same email. This anchors the payment timeline to the delivery date, not the approval date.</li>
          <li><strong>Set net-15 terms, not net-30</strong> &mdash; shorter payment terms reduce cash flow gaps. Most brands accept net-15 when asked. Do not assume net-30 is standard just because larger companies default to it.</li>
          <li><strong>Follow up on day 16</strong> &mdash; if net-15 passes without payment, send a polite reminder the next day. Waiting longer signals that you are flexible on payment timing.</li>
          <li><strong>Track everything in one place</strong> &mdash; use a spreadsheet or Wave's dashboard. Know exactly how much you are owed, by whom, and when it is due.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 05 Contracts & Legal -->
