      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">05 &mdash; Contracts &amp; Legal</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Contracts and legal protection</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Never deliver content without a signed agreement on usage rights</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">E-signature tools make contracts frictionless for both sides</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Usage rights, payment terms, and revision limits are the three non-negotiable clauses</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Contracts protect both the creator and the brand. They define what content is being produced, who owns it, how it can be used, and what happens when things go sideways. Operating without contracts is the fastest way to lose money and control over your own content.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The most common dispute OKAD mediates between brands and creators involves usage rights. A creator delivers a video assuming it will be used in one Instagram ad. The brand runs it across TikTok, YouTube, Facebook, and their website for 18 months. Without a contract specifying scope, the creator has no recourse.</p>

