        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Three clauses every UGC contract needs</h3>
        <ol class="list-none p-0 counter-reset-step space-y-0">
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Usage rights.</strong> Specify exactly which platforms, for how long, and whether the content can be used in paid ads. Unlimited perpetual usage across all platforms should cost significantly more than a single organic post on one account.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Payment terms.</strong> Amount, currency, payment method, due date. Include late payment penalties &mdash; even a small one signals that you take payment seriously and discourages delays.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Revision limits.</strong> Define how many rounds of revisions are included. Two rounds is standard. Additional revisions should trigger additional fees. Without this clause, brands can request unlimited changes on a flat-fee contract.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
