        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">The metrics that actually matter</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Forget follower counts and like totals. The metrics that determine whether your content works &mdash; and whether brands rehire you &mdash; are:</p>
        <ul class="pl-5 mb-4 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
          <li><strong><a href="/hook-rate" class="text-accent hover:underline">Hook rate</a></strong> &mdash; percentage of viewers who watch past the first 3 seconds. This measures whether your opening grabs attention. Target: 40%+ for strong performance.</li>
          <li><strong>Watch-through rate</strong> &mdash; percentage who watch the entire video. Measures whether your content holds attention after the hook. Target: 25%+ for 30-second videos.</li>
          <li><strong>Share and save rate</strong> &mdash; saves indicate intent; shares indicate endorsement. Both signal content that resonates beyond passive viewing.</li>
          <li><strong>Conversion (if available)</strong> &mdash; click-through rate, link clicks, profile visits. When brands share this data, it is the most direct measure of content effectiveness.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">OKAD recommends that creators maintain a simple Google Sheet tracking each video's format, hook type, niche, and key metrics. Over time, patterns emerge: certain hooks outperform others, certain formats convert better for specific industries, and your best work clusters around recognizable patterns. This data is what turns you from a replaceable creator into a strategic asset.</p>
